{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793438436,"nonce":"RstptR/cGUISdb4Yfgzj9gyZIng=","title":"Lua method_call: where the 15x behind LuaJIT goes","message":"CI 9f18acb1, Linux: zylua 110.8 ms wall / 34.1 ms timed, LuaJIT 7.4 / 6.1; macOS 72.6 / 21.2 against 9.4 / 5.5. Three quarters of the wall is before the timed loop starts.\n\nBefore the loop (Mac trace, ZYNTAX_TRACE_LAZY, timestamps from spawn): main at 6 ms, parse and lowering done at 18 ms (lowering 8.4, of which 6 ms is bodies with 244 adopted library functions). The warm-up thread then optimises the small methods (Toggle.new, both activates, value, the which finders, about 8 ms) before it starts on lua$chunk, which the main thread is already waiting for (static-hot). The chunk takes 34 ms: 25 ms of body over four rounds (the fourth finds nothing) and 7 to 8 ms of Cranelift. The first call waits 24 to 31 ms.\n\nThe loop itself, split into one variant per loop (loaded Mac, timed ms, zylua / LuaJIT in the same run): Toggle loop 7.2 / 2.0, NthToggle loop 15.3 / 4.9.\n- Every `obj:activate()` and `:value()` calls a `which` finder (lua$which$1$activate, 88 HIR insts; which$1$value 62) that walks the own slot, the metatable and `__index` to choose the function, since nothing proves the instances never gain their own `activate`. Finder plus method per site fills lua$chunk's 2000-instruction budget after about half the 40 sites; the rest stay calls (ZYNTAX_TRACE_INLINE: 103 refusals of which$1$value, 96 of which$1$activate on the caller budget).\n- NthToggle.new builds the object with Toggle.new and then stores `count_max` and `count`, so those keys are not born slots of the shape: NthToggle:activate reads and writes them through zl_setindex_key with zb_box_i64, and at 142 insts it is refused as too large at every site.\n- A variant with one site per loop and ten times the iterations inlines every finder and is only about 10% faster (same loaded Mac), so the budget is the smaller part; what remains is the finder walk itself, inlined or not, and the hash-part fields.\n\nDirections: fold a method lookup to a metatable guard when no store can give an instance of the shape that key and the class table's slot is not reassigned after it is built; let stores made right after construction in the constructing function (after setmetatable) extend the shape; have the worker start on a static-hot function the main thread waits for before anything else.","files":null}]}